CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!lock->owner"
#263: FILE: kernel/locking/rwsem-xadd.c:303:
+	return lock->owner == NULL;

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'count > RWSEM_WAITING_BIAS'
#367: FILE: kernel/locking/rwsem-xadd.c:400:
+	if ((count > RWSEM_WAITING_BIAS) && waiting)

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

